            <ArticleTitle>Right ventricular outflow tract thrombus in a case of Behcet's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>380-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Behcet's disease is known as a chronic systemic vasculitic syndrome, the hallmark of which is recurrent oral aphthous and genital ulcerations and uveitis. Vascular involvement, mainly thrombosis, reportedly affects as many as one-third of patients. Cardiac involvement, however, is very rare. We present in this report a young female patient developing right ventricular thrombus while being treated medically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
